cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation artifacts, please cite it as below."
title: "answerdesk: a reproducible multilingual customer-support RAG reference stack"
abstract: >-
  A local-first, MIT-licensed reference implementation of multilingual customer-support RAG with
  span-verified citations, a split-conformal answer/escalate decision under a cost model, a guarded
  semantic cache, an operator console showing the decision, and a reproducible evaluation harness
  (frozen hashed splits, paired bootstrap, McNemar, judge calibration protocol). Ships its negative
  results: risk control did not hold on the first live study.
authors:
  - name: "answerdesk contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/answerdesk/answerdesk"
url: "https://github.com/answerdesk/answerdesk"
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - customer support
  - multilingual
  - conformal prediction
  - calibrated abstention
  - citation verification
  - semantic cache
  - reproducible evaluation
  - uv
  - python
